<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Francia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francia">Francia</a> was the eastern kingdom created when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> was divided by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-verdun">Treaty of Verdun</a> in 843, initially under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a>. Covering much of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, it developed into the Kingdom of Germany and became the core of the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-francia.jpg" alt="East Francia" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blank map of Europe.svg: maix¿? derivative work: Alphathon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Francia_843.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
